1
00:00:00,766 --> 00:00:04,766
[bright music]

2
00:00:25,821 --> 00:00:29,821
[bright music]

3
00:00:36,916 --> 00:00:39,166
What are you doing, bestfriend?

4
00:00:39,208 --> 00:00:40,833
Are you listening to me?

5
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:43,374
I’m preparing food for work later.

6
00:00:43,416 --> 00:00:45,291
Cost-cutting measures.

7
00:00:45,708 --> 00:00:47,500
I'm leaving in a while.

8
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:51,125
Did you reach out to
the festival organizers?

9
00:00:51,375 --> 00:00:53,958
They might know the scammer!

10
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:55,666
Yes, I sent them an e-mail.

11
00:00:55,708 --> 00:00:57,291
Did they reply?

12
00:00:57,333 --> 00:01:00,041
They said they’re not
related with the scammer.

13
00:01:00,083 --> 00:01:02,249
They didn’t even know who he is.

14
00:01:02,291 --> 00:01:04,999
They said I should file a police report.

15
00:01:05,041 --> 00:01:07,916
Why don’t you post it on
social media, bestfriend?

16
00:01:08,125 --> 00:01:11,416
That way the scammer will be exposed!

17
00:01:11,458 --> 00:01:12,749
No!

18
00:01:12,791 --> 00:01:14,958
It will spread like wildfire!

19
00:01:15,166 --> 00:01:17,500
People like you love to gossip.

20
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:20,208
And I don’t want mom to worry.

21
00:01:20,916 --> 00:01:23,150
I don’t want her to find
out that I threw away

22
00:01:23,192 --> 00:01:25,375
all her savings for
that stupid membership.

23
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,291
If I were there, I would
kick him in the butt!

24
00:01:29,250 --> 00:01:30,958
What now, bestfriend?

25
00:01:31,291 --> 00:01:33,416
When is your flight back home?

26
00:01:34,208 --> 00:01:36,125
You’re about to start another film, right?

27
00:01:36,666 --> 00:01:38,124
In two days.

28
00:01:38,166 --> 00:01:41,125
But I might extend my stay here.

29
00:01:41,791 --> 00:01:45,000
I don’t want to go back home
without my mom’s savings.

30
00:01:45,166 --> 00:01:47,666
I won’t stop until I find that swindler.

31
00:01:47,875 --> 00:01:50,291
Bestfriend, if you need anything,

32
00:01:50,333 --> 00:01:52,083
I’ll be glad to help.

33
00:01:52,625 --> 00:01:55,916
I can send you 2,000 pesos.

34
00:01:56,333 --> 00:01:58,166
I know that’s not a lot.

35
00:01:58,208 --> 00:02:01,708
But at least, you’ll have
some money to buy Jollibee.

36
00:02:02,083 --> 00:02:04,249
Wait, is there even a Jollibee store there?

37
00:02:04,291 --> 00:02:06,125
Yeap, there is.

38
00:02:06,416 --> 00:02:07,624
And thank you so much, besfriend.

39
00:02:07,666 --> 00:02:09,291
But keep your money.

40
00:02:09,333 --> 00:02:10,666
I’ll be fine.

41
00:02:12,708 --> 00:02:14,374
Sorry, bestfriend.

42
00:02:14,416 --> 00:02:16,374
My roommate’s going to use the bathroom.

43
00:02:16,416 --> 00:02:17,583
I’ll talk to you later.

44
00:02:17,625 --> 00:02:19,416
Bye, bestfriend.

45
00:02:20,963 --> 00:02:22,624
[door opens]

46
00:02:22,666 --> 00:02:25,416
You know the bathroom
has more important purposes

47
00:02:25,458 --> 00:02:28,000
than making long phone calls, yeah?

48
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:30,041
Sorry.

49
00:02:35,291 --> 00:02:38,083
Uh, hey, can I ask you something?

50
00:02:38,750 --> 00:02:40,041
What?

51
00:02:40,250 --> 00:02:42,708
Do you know where I can
find some work here in LA?

52
00:02:42,750 --> 00:02:43,958
Why are you looking for work?

53
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,833
I thought you have a very
exclusive Hollywood project lined up?

54
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,916
Oh, uh, yeah.

55
00:02:48,958 --> 00:02:50,791
No, of course, um...

56
00:02:50,833 --> 00:02:53,958
I just got an update from
the Hollywood Executive today

57
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,708
and it’s going great, uh, great stuff.

58
00:02:56,750 --> 00:02:57,791
Cool.

59
00:02:57,833 --> 00:03:00,791
So why are you looking for work?

60
00:03:01,541 --> 00:03:04,708
Oh, well, you know,
production hasn’t yet started

61
00:03:04,750 --> 00:03:08,333
and I just thought I would make
myself busy in the meantime.

62
00:03:08,875 --> 00:03:12,375
Uh, do you know any
other Filipinos here in LA?

63
00:03:13,291 --> 00:03:14,166
No.

64
00:03:14,291 --> 00:03:16,333
Okay, I don’t think I can help you.

65
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:20,416
Okay, well, um, if you think
of anyone or something…

66
00:03:20,458 --> 00:03:22,583
I’m in a rush. I have to get to work.

67
00:03:22,625 --> 00:03:25,708
By the way, uh, my name is Andre.

68
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:27,249
What was your name again?

69
00:03:27,291 --> 00:03:28,583
Joshua.

70
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:31,499
Thanks, Joshua. I really appreciate it.

71
00:03:31,541 --> 00:03:33,083
Appreciate what?

72
00:03:33,125 --> 00:03:34,772
For helping me out.

73
00:03:34,814 --> 00:03:35,749
[bright music]

74
00:03:35,791 --> 00:03:37,874
No one’s helping you out.

75
00:03:37,916 --> 00:03:40,541
You only get to stay here for one
week because you gave me $300.

76
00:03:40,583 --> 00:03:43,041
If you give me another 300,
you can stay here another week.

77
00:03:43,083 --> 00:03:45,874
That’s it. No more, no less.

78
00:03:45,916 --> 00:03:49,000
Besides, I’m just after
your money, remember?

79
00:03:49,333 --> 00:03:50,999
Can we please let that one pass?

80
00:03:51,041 --> 00:03:53,958
I said I was sorry, and if I could take
my words back, I absolutely would.

81
00:03:54,000 --> 00:03:56,999
Yeah, the thing about words is

82
00:03:57,041 --> 00:03:59,583
there’s no way to take them
back once you’ve said them.

83
00:03:59,625 --> 00:04:01,583
Uh, so unless you’ve got cash,

84
00:04:01,625 --> 00:04:03,625
we have nothing to talk about.

85
00:04:04,333 --> 00:04:07,000
Six days and you’re out.

86
00:04:16,120 --> 00:04:20,120
[bright music]

87
00:04:27,125 --> 00:04:28,041
What?

88
00:04:28,083 --> 00:04:31,666
Oh, sorry. I was just wondering, um…

89
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:33,374
What?

90
00:04:33,416 --> 00:04:36,291
Oh if… if you knew where
the spare keys were.

91
00:04:36,333 --> 00:04:37,166
I, um,

92
00:04:37,208 --> 00:04:38,249
I might go out later.

93
00:04:38,291 --> 00:04:39,708
Oh, yeah.

94
00:04:41,583 --> 00:04:42,833
Sorry, Van.

95
00:04:43,250 --> 00:04:44,500
I forgot.

96
00:04:45,291 --> 00:04:46,291
Van?

97
00:04:47,666 --> 00:04:48,541
What?

98
00:04:48,625 --> 00:04:49,958
You… you just called me Van.

99
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:51,625
My name is Andre.

100
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:53,208
I know.

101
00:04:53,250 --> 00:04:55,000
So, who’s Van?

102
00:04:56,083 --> 00:04:57,250
No one.

103
00:04:57,791 --> 00:04:59,250
I’m bad at names.

104
00:05:02,291 --> 00:05:03,375
Alright.

105
00:05:04,250 --> 00:05:05,583
Your keys are here.

106
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:09,416
Do you have any other questions?

107
00:05:10,291 --> 00:05:10,958
No.

108
00:05:12,468 --> 00:05:15,833
[bright music]

109
00:05:15,875 --> 00:05:17,125
Thanks, Josh.

110
00:05:18,750 --> 00:05:21,333
Excuse me. What did you just call me?

111
00:05:21,750 --> 00:05:23,375
Uh, Josh?

112
00:05:23,458 --> 00:05:26,333
I thought I told you my name is Joshua.

113
00:05:26,375 --> 00:05:28,083
And isn’t Josh short for Joshua?

114
00:05:28,125 --> 00:05:30,708
I didn't give you permission
to call me by that name.

115
00:05:30,750 --> 00:05:33,416
Sorry. I didn't think I need
permission to call you Josh

116
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:36,750
since it’s pretty much the
universal short name for Joshua.

117
00:05:37,208 --> 00:05:39,375
And you just called me
Van like two minutes ago.

118
00:05:39,666 --> 00:05:41,166
Whatever.

119
00:05:41,208 --> 00:05:42,249
Six days.

120
00:05:42,291 --> 00:05:43,500
And you're out.

121
00:05:45,333 --> 00:05:46,291
Whatever.

122
00:05:46,333 --> 00:05:48,208
Six days. And you're out.

123
00:05:48,583 --> 00:05:50,500
I didn't give you permission
to call me Joshua.

124
00:05:51,208 --> 00:05:52,666
Geez!

125
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:56,458
Coming from somebody who doesn’t
want to be called selfish and greedy.

126
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:00,750
Oh, hi Josh...

127
00:06:01,708 --> 00:06:02,749
...ua.

128
00:06:02,791 --> 00:06:04,833
Are you talking to yourself?

129
00:06:05,833 --> 00:06:07,833
No, uh, I was just practicing.

130
00:06:07,875 --> 00:06:09,791
I have a rehearsal later, so...

131
00:06:10,208 --> 00:06:11,708
Whatever.

132
00:06:12,291 --> 00:06:14,875
Six days. And you're out.

133
00:06:17,997 --> 00:06:21,997
[bright music]

134
00:06:26,750 --> 00:06:27,350
Oh.

135
00:06:28,083 --> 00:06:29,708
What the hell are you doing?

136
00:06:30,625 --> 00:06:31,167
I was...

137
00:06:31,209 --> 00:06:33,041
I was just, um, looking for my…

138
00:06:33,083 --> 00:06:34,374
my underwear,

139
00:06:34,416 --> 00:06:35,583
which is, um...

140
00:06:35,625 --> 00:06:37,125
You're holding it.

141
00:06:40,291 --> 00:06:42,083
Yeah, yeah, um…

142
00:06:42,291 --> 00:06:44,041
I just... Sorry, I'm just...

143
00:06:44,083 --> 00:06:45,500
Let’s take a shower.

144
00:06:45,625 --> 00:06:46,333
I...

145
00:06:46,375 --> 00:06:47,833
I mean I'm...

146
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:49,708
I'm going to take a shower.

147
00:06:49,750 --> 00:06:51,833
Not… not you and…

148
00:06:52,333 --> 00:06:54,125
I’m… I’m gonna…

149
00:06:54,333 --> 00:06:55,708
Okay, I’m gonna go.

150
00:07:04,167 --> 00:07:08,167
[bright music]

151
00:07:33,367 --> 00:07:37,367
[piano music]

152
00:07:42,500 --> 00:07:43,583
Hello, who’s this?

153
00:07:43,625 --> 00:07:44,749
You didn’t save my number?

154
00:07:44,791 --> 00:07:46,458
Why would I? I don't know you.

155
00:07:46,500 --> 00:07:48,666
I'm the greedy, selfish guy
who's just after your money.

156
00:07:48,708 --> 00:07:49,624
Oh, yeah, yeah.

157
00:07:49,666 --> 00:07:50,499
Yes, you are.

158
00:07:50,541 --> 00:07:52,458
Or not that you’re greedy and selfish,

159
00:07:52,500 --> 00:07:55,749
just that you’re my kind
and caring roommate.

160
00:07:55,791 --> 00:07:57,708
Anyway, sorry I didn’t save
your number. It's just that -

161
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:58,833
Yeah, I don’t care about that.

162
00:07:58,875 --> 00:08:01,250
Um, I just wanted to
ask, are you free tonight?

163
00:08:01,333 --> 00:08:04,916
Uh, are you asking me out on a…

164
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:06,708
What the hell are you talking about?

165
00:08:06,833 --> 00:08:07,791
Easy, easy, okay?

166
00:08:07,833 --> 00:08:10,333
I just thought maybe
you’re asking me out as a...

167
00:08:10,416 --> 00:08:11,249
friend.

168
00:08:11,291 --> 00:08:12,291
We're not friends.

169
00:08:12,333 --> 00:08:14,291
And I don't need company,
especially not with you.

170
00:08:14,333 --> 00:08:15,249
Okay, so why –

171
00:08:15,291 --> 00:08:16,666
I got something for you.

172
00:08:16,708 --> 00:08:18,416
Like a gift?

173
00:08:18,458 --> 00:08:20,208
No, why would I do that?

174
00:08:20,250 --> 00:08:21,499
You just said you got me something.

175
00:08:21,541 --> 00:08:22,708
I got a gig.

176
00:08:22,750 --> 00:08:23,458
Oh.

177
00:08:24,250 --> 00:08:25,041
Really?

178
00:08:25,083 --> 00:08:28,791
Yeah, um, let’s see. It’s four hours.

179
00:08:28,833 --> 00:08:30,291
Uh, 50 bucks.

180
00:08:30,333 --> 00:08:32,249
50 dollars? Hold on.

181
00:08:32,291 --> 00:08:34,416
2,500 pesos?

182
00:08:35,041 --> 00:08:36,291
Oh, yeah, yeah, sure. I’m free.

183
00:08:36,333 --> 00:08:37,708
I’m definitely free.

184
00:08:37,750 --> 00:08:39,291
Okay, I’ll text you the location.

185
00:08:39,333 --> 00:08:40,583
Yeah, okay. I’ll be there.

186
00:08:40,625 --> 00:08:42,500
And I just wanna say…

187
00:08:43,791 --> 00:08:45,083
Hello?

188
00:08:47,250 --> 00:08:50,333
I just wanna say thank
you for thinking about me.

189
00:08:56,028 --> 00:09:00,028
[bright music]

190
00:09:13,375 --> 00:09:15,166
Hi, son. How are you?

191
00:09:15,250 --> 00:09:16,125
Uh...

192
00:09:16,458 --> 00:09:18,833
I’m okay. How about you?

193
00:09:19,208 --> 00:09:23,791
I’m not feeling well.

194
00:09:24,458 --> 00:09:25,083
What?

195
00:09:25,791 --> 00:09:26,708
Are you okay?

196
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:28,458
Did you go to the doctor?

197
00:09:28,541 --> 00:09:30,708
No need.

198
00:09:31,291 --> 00:09:35,374
I’ll take some medicines, get some rest,

199
00:09:35,416 --> 00:09:37,208
then go back to work.

200
00:09:37,250 --> 00:09:38,875
But you’re sick, mom.

201
00:09:39,750 --> 00:09:42,916
Don’t worry about me.

202
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:44,708
I’m fine.

203
00:09:44,875 --> 00:09:48,416
Let’s talk about you. How has it been?

204
00:09:48,750 --> 00:09:51,708
By the way, I saw a post on Facebook.

205
00:09:51,750 --> 00:09:53,708
Did you win another award?

206
00:09:53,750 --> 00:09:57,416
Yes, mom. Grand Jury
Award for my short film.

207
00:09:57,458 --> 00:09:59,833
Wow! Congrats, son!

208
00:09:59,875 --> 00:10:02,124
Every time I hear your achievements,

209
00:10:02,166 --> 00:10:04,750
all my stress and anxiety disappear.

210
00:10:05,541 --> 00:10:08,833
Then, you will start another film project

211
00:10:08,875 --> 00:10:10,541
when you go back to the Philippines?

212
00:10:10,583 --> 00:10:12,624
Yes, mom. My script got selected.

213
00:10:12,666 --> 00:10:15,333
They’ll give initial
funding for my new film.

214
00:10:16,500 --> 00:10:18,416
I don’t know what to say, son.

215
00:10:18,458 --> 00:10:20,416
You’re amazing!

216
00:10:21,666 --> 00:10:23,249
But where are you headed now?

217
00:10:23,291 --> 00:10:24,833
Why are you dressed up?

218
00:10:24,875 --> 00:10:26,458
I have a gig, mom.

219
00:10:26,666 --> 00:10:28,124
Look at you.

220
00:10:28,166 --> 00:10:31,458
Just a few days in America
and you already got a gig?

221
00:10:32,041 --> 00:10:34,750
Son, in case you need to buy anything,

222
00:10:34,916 --> 00:10:37,708
just spend the money I’ve
been sending you, okay?

223
00:10:38,208 --> 00:10:40,333
Don’t worry about it.

224
00:10:40,375 --> 00:10:42,916
It’s just money.

225
00:10:42,958 --> 00:10:44,874
I’m concerned about you.

226
00:10:44,916 --> 00:10:46,958
Everything is so expensive there.

227
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:49,666
You’re spending in dollars, not pesos.

228
00:10:50,791 --> 00:10:54,708
Mom, the truth is…

229
00:10:54,750 --> 00:10:56,195
What is it, son?

230
00:10:56,237 --> 00:10:59,708
[piano music]

231
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:01,916
I received an offer here.

232
00:11:01,958 --> 00:11:03,666
From a Hollywood Executive.

233
00:11:03,708 --> 00:11:04,833
Really?

234
00:11:04,875 --> 00:11:08,250
That’s the best news I’ve heard!

235
00:11:08,458 --> 00:11:11,166
Thank you, Lord!

236
00:11:11,416 --> 00:11:16,166
Suddenly, my fever is gone.

237
00:11:16,916 --> 00:11:19,124
I’m very happy for you.

238
00:11:19,166 --> 00:11:22,500
You’re slowly achieving your dreams.

239
00:11:24,083 --> 00:11:25,666
Okay, son.

240
00:11:26,041 --> 00:11:29,208
I don’t want to keep you
from your appointment.

241
00:11:29,458 --> 00:11:32,208
I’ll call you again next time.

242
00:11:34,541 --> 00:11:35,208
Okay, mom.

243
00:11:35,250 --> 00:11:36,833
Love you.

244
00:11:37,125 --> 00:11:38,833
Okay, love you too.

245
00:11:38,875 --> 00:11:40,666
Always take care, okay?

246
00:11:40,708 --> 00:11:41,916
Bye.

247
00:11:48,710 --> 00:11:52,710
[footsteps]

248
00:11:56,958 --> 00:11:58,875
Gig in a liquor store?

249
00:12:00,125 --> 00:12:02,458
Or maybe this is just a meeting place?

250
00:12:07,413 --> 00:12:11,413
[street noise]

251
00:12:14,750 --> 00:12:15,833
Oh.

252
00:12:15,916 --> 00:12:18,000
Hi, Josh... ua.

253
00:12:22,125 --> 00:12:25,333
Are you going to the Oscars or something?

254
00:12:25,833 --> 00:12:28,541
No, I’m here for the gig you told me about.

255
00:12:29,791 --> 00:12:31,541
Why? Am I late?

256
00:12:31,583 --> 00:12:33,374
- Or is it cancelled? - No, no.

257
00:12:33,416 --> 00:12:34,875
Why, why this?

258
00:12:35,791 --> 00:12:38,666
Well, I assumed it has
something to do with an event.

259
00:12:38,708 --> 00:12:39,999
We’re in LA, right?

260
00:12:40,041 --> 00:12:42,166
Everything here is
about events and parties?

261
00:12:42,208 --> 00:12:44,000
Where did you get that idea?

262
00:12:45,083 --> 00:12:46,041
Here.

263
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:50,000
I need you to take these out. I’m
gonna show you how to use the register.

264
00:12:50,750 --> 00:12:51,750
Oh.

265
00:12:52,125 --> 00:12:54,708
So I’m going to be a…

266
00:12:54,750 --> 00:12:56,333
Sorry to disappoint you.

267
00:12:56,375 --> 00:12:59,166
I mean, this is not, uh,

268
00:12:59,208 --> 00:13:01,249
an awards ceremony.

269
00:13:01,291 --> 00:13:02,458
If you don’t want to…

270
00:13:02,500 --> 00:13:05,416
No, no, I didn’t mean to say…

271
00:13:05,458 --> 00:13:06,499
I just...

272
00:13:06,541 --> 00:13:08,041
I just wish you had told me sooner.

273
00:13:08,083 --> 00:13:09,333
But, um...

274
00:13:09,583 --> 00:13:10,958
Yeah, no, it's...

275
00:13:11,541 --> 00:13:15,666
What gave you the idea
that I do parties or events?

276
00:13:15,958 --> 00:13:18,166
Well, you always come home late at night.

277
00:13:18,208 --> 00:13:19,083
Okay.

278
00:13:19,125 --> 00:13:23,791
What if I’m a caretaker for a
family and I have late night shifts?

279
00:13:23,833 --> 00:13:26,791
What if I’m a waiter? Or a
movie theater employee?

280
00:13:26,833 --> 00:13:29,250
I don’t know how you’re
gonna work dressed like that.

281
00:13:30,041 --> 00:13:32,666
No, it’s fine. Don’t worry about it.

282
00:13:33,672 --> 00:13:37,672
[bright music]

283
00:13:41,416 --> 00:13:43,833
See? Problem solved.

284
00:13:44,333 --> 00:13:48,041
Now, uh, where do I put these?

285
00:13:50,958 --> 00:13:52,916
So look at the price tag
attached to every item

286
00:13:52,958 --> 00:13:54,666
and for card transactions,

287
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:58,291
just have people insert
or swipe right here.

288
00:13:58,875 --> 00:13:59,499
That’s it?

289
00:13:59,541 --> 00:14:01,083
Yeah, that’s it.

290
00:14:01,125 --> 00:14:02,666
I’ll be back by 10.

291
00:14:02,750 --> 00:14:04,416
Where are you going?

292
00:14:05,833 --> 00:14:07,625
None of your business.

293
00:14:07,916 --> 00:14:10,958
- Oh, you’re going on a date.
- Just do your work

294
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:13,416
and only call me if you need something.

295
00:14:13,791 --> 00:14:14,875
Got it.

296
00:14:16,125 --> 00:14:18,208
Oh, by the way,

297
00:14:18,375 --> 00:14:19,625
take care.

298
00:14:20,291 --> 00:14:21,916
Will you stop being so…

299
00:14:21,958 --> 00:14:22,708
So?

300
00:14:22,750 --> 00:14:23,916
Annoying.

301
00:14:23,958 --> 00:14:26,416
Me saying take care annoys you?

302
00:14:26,458 --> 00:14:28,458
I say take care to all of my friends.

303
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:32,249
I’ll say this again.

304
00:14:32,291 --> 00:14:35,249
We’re not friends.

305
00:14:35,291 --> 00:14:36,874
We’re roommates.

306
00:14:36,916 --> 00:14:37,999
Fine.

307
00:14:38,041 --> 00:14:41,250
To my roommate who refuses to be my friend,

308
00:14:41,416 --> 00:14:43,000
take care.

309
00:14:45,098 --> 00:14:49,098
[bright music]

310
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:05,458
Hi. How can I help you?

311
00:15:05,500 --> 00:15:06,666
Marlboros.

312
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:08,666
Come again?

313
00:15:09,041 --> 00:15:11,291
Can I get some Marlboros? Are you deaf?

314
00:15:15,041 --> 00:15:16,791
You can remove it.

315
00:15:19,250 --> 00:15:20,916
Fucking Asian.

316
00:15:21,041 --> 00:15:23,000
Excuse me, what did you just call me?

317
00:15:23,125 --> 00:15:24,583
I said fucking Asian.

318
00:15:24,625 --> 00:15:25,999
Do you have a problem with that?

319
00:15:26,041 --> 00:15:26,874
Yeah.

320
00:15:26,916 --> 00:15:28,333
Maybe I do.

321
00:15:31,666 --> 00:15:32,958
I'm back.

322
00:15:35,875 --> 00:15:36,833
Andre?

323
00:15:42,208 --> 00:15:43,666
Hello?

324
00:15:46,875 --> 00:15:48,500
Where are you?

325
00:16:00,166 --> 00:16:02,041
What happened to your face?

326
00:16:09,833 --> 00:16:13,416
Are you sure you don’t want
to report the incident, or...

327
00:16:14,625 --> 00:16:16,749
Um, no, it’s fine.

328
00:16:16,791 --> 00:16:17,708
I don't wanna...

329
00:16:17,750 --> 00:16:19,375
I don't wanna make a scene.

330
00:16:20,875 --> 00:16:22,958
Have you eaten anything yet tonight?

331
00:16:24,041 --> 00:16:25,708
I'm okay.

332
00:16:27,875 --> 00:16:29,708
I’ll fix you something.

333
00:16:30,166 --> 00:16:33,249
- No, you really don’t have to.
- Just sit down. Wait.

334
00:16:33,291 --> 00:16:34,958
- But I - - Stop.

335
00:16:35,166 --> 00:16:36,625
Just stop.

336
00:16:54,541 --> 00:16:57,291
You have to be extra
careful out there, okay?

337
00:16:57,666 --> 00:16:59,083
It’s not safe.

338
00:17:02,613 --> 00:17:06,613
[footsteps]

339
00:17:25,666 --> 00:17:26,833
Kimchi.

340
00:17:27,583 --> 00:17:29,291
Why? You don’t like it?

341
00:17:30,041 --> 00:17:31,583
Nah, are you kidding me?

342
00:17:31,625 --> 00:17:33,458
Korean food’s my favorite.

343
00:17:33,500 --> 00:17:36,916
Well, after adobo and sinigang, of course.

344
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,208
Hmm... and rice too!

345
00:17:41,416 --> 00:17:42,749
You know,

346
00:17:42,791 --> 00:17:46,291
this is starting to look and
feel like a real K-drama.

347
00:17:46,791 --> 00:17:48,333
Do you watch K-dramas?

348
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:51,166
They’re very popular in Asia,

349
00:17:51,208 --> 00:17:52,874
especially in the Philippines.

350
00:17:52,916 --> 00:17:54,333
Shut up and eat.

351
00:17:54,375 --> 00:17:56,134
And they’re good too, huh.

352
00:17:56,176 --> 00:17:57,833
[bright music]

353
00:17:57,875 --> 00:17:59,666
Oh, you’re not gonna eat with me?

354
00:17:59,708 --> 00:18:00,666
No.

355
00:18:02,875 --> 00:18:05,458
Well, if this were a real K-drama,

356
00:18:05,500 --> 00:18:07,333
we would definitely be eating together.

357
00:18:07,375 --> 00:18:09,333
Especially after I got hurt.

358
00:18:09,375 --> 00:18:12,166
This would be the part where
the two main characters -

359
00:18:12,208 --> 00:18:14,166
We’re not in a Korean drama.

360
00:18:14,708 --> 00:18:16,500
Stop being cheesy.

361
00:18:18,708 --> 00:18:21,500
You’ll take back your words
if you actually watch K-drama.

362
00:18:22,166 --> 00:18:23,791
But this looks good.

363
00:18:23,833 --> 00:18:25,875
Thank you.

364
00:18:29,000 --> 00:18:29,750
Oh.

365
00:18:36,833 --> 00:18:38,041
50 dollars,

366
00:18:38,083 --> 00:18:39,583
a nice and caring roommate,

367
00:18:39,625 --> 00:18:41,125
and a delicious meal.

368
00:18:44,916 --> 00:18:46,250
And you know,

369
00:18:46,500 --> 00:18:48,291
if this were a K-drama,

370
00:18:48,750 --> 00:18:51,291
this would be the part
where you treat my wound.

371
00:18:52,083 --> 00:18:55,208
And you stare into my eyes,

372
00:18:55,416 --> 00:18:58,166
then you slowly, ever so slowly realize...

373
00:18:58,208 --> 00:19:00,291
Okay, well, there’s ice in the freezer,

374
00:19:00,333 --> 00:19:02,208
if you wanna go grab that.

375
00:19:02,250 --> 00:19:03,666
Don’t you wanna get it for me?

376
00:19:03,708 --> 00:19:06,666
And just put it on my eye gently.

377
00:19:06,708 --> 00:19:09,041
- Put it on my face. - What the hell? No.

378
00:19:09,541 --> 00:19:10,583
But...

379
00:19:11,125 --> 00:19:13,083
But it hurts so much.

380
00:19:13,500 --> 00:19:15,125
It's so painful.

381
00:19:17,250 --> 00:19:18,791
Oh my God.

382
00:19:20,693 --> 00:19:24,541
[bright music]

383
00:19:24,583 --> 00:19:27,166
Fine. Maybe I’m not a good actor.

384
00:19:45,243 --> 00:19:49,243
[bright music]
